#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138083 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138428 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f80bc47-7b56-5357-b4e7-718f4ddfa41b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution to a System From Its Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "cbf28a0c-c34d-5855-b72e-4225a11710c1" :question/math-academy-id "e-13129" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=8 \\\\ 2x-y=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the diagram below to determine this system's solution $(x,y)$.\n\n![](images/6f/6f0b7960b9b4c98250741b009da2ad19c1123c5b7adf9cd5072430fb9a879dc9.png)" :question/worked-solution "The solution of the system corresponds to the point of intersection of the lines. \n\n![](images/5c/5c1c69adc880ea7cfdb5a4e0a10abd6032d2eedf0386923b94df9b7c173edd6d.png)\n\nIn this case, we have the point $(4,2).$ Therefore, the solution to the given system is $(4,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138084 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138429 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4154d81b-c94a-57f7-80fa-0daa341505e6" :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems"}] :question/id #uuid "86771ced-afc0-5061-a532-bc2345a52ea8" :question/math-academy-id "e-13130" :question/problem "![](images/09/0915c99015922e27855d92ebb13756da634a8f10dd8fe3abbc016590f06e1077.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the number of liters of water in pool $A$ and pool $B$ as a function of time, measured in days. How many days will it take for both pools to contain the same amount of water?" :question/worked-solution "The pools have the same amount of water when the two graphs intersect.\n\n![](images/cf/cf7a9b8bdccbc66086c473813523ed893ee192830965300a8c4a0702ad065fc3.png)\n\nIn this case, we have the point $(5,400).$ So, both pools have the same amount ($400\\,\\textrm{L}$) of water at $t=5$ days."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495118 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138429 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4154d81b-c94a-57f7-80fa-0daa341505e